Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
search GroupFields UnitTests Utilities list;
define
    lamp isRule defer
        ask   isRule q-="value?" defer code={ cerr "   >>> lamp ask FIRED":; };
    cdMatch  code={ v = 0; if lamp("value?"); v = 1; cerr "CD-1 match verdict = " v:; };
    cdFail   code={ v = 0; if lamp("fly"); v = 1; cerr "CD-2 failure verdict = " v:; };
    cdPrefix code={ v = 0; if lamp("value? junk"); v = 1; cerr "CD-3 prefix verdict = " v:; };
    ;
cdMatch();
cdFail();
cerr "CD-4 window closed after the failed drive":;
cdPrefix();
cerr "CONVDRIVE SENTINEL":;
stop();

convDriveT -- a field parses a message against its own small grammar. Born 2026-09-23,
Clay's conversation step 1, Tony's ruling that this comes ahead of F-110.

lamp is a rule whose members are its vocabulary; driving lamp("...") parses the text
against lamp's grammar only. Root AND member are marked defer, so a matching member's
action PARKS on the returned label instead of firing during the drive. That parking is
measured, 2026-09-23: runRule hands back ask's label retagged lamp, deferred=1, gMethod
processAction, text "gask". The gate is fireLabelMethod's `deferred && held`: a deferred
root alone does NOT park an undeferred member, which fires during the drive.

Rows, read by genLadder/pop.sh:
  CD-1  control  lamp("value?") matches -> verdict 1, and ask does NOT fire (parked).
        Negative control, run by hand 2026-09-23: with defer removed from the member,
        ask fires twice in this file (match and prefix) instead of zero times.
  CD-2  control  lamp("fly") fails -> verdict 0. CD-1's non-zero sibling.
  CD-3  RED BY DESIGN  lamp("value? junk") must NOT read as a full match. Today it does
        (verdict 1): only a prefix has to match and the junk is dropped silently. Goes
        green with step 2, the verdict's consumed length.
  CD-4  RED BY DESIGN  the failed drive must produce a named "does not understand" line.
        Today a failure is silent. Goes green with step 3, the default handler.

Each verdict is read with `if lamp(...)` INSIDE an action. A top-level `x := lamp(...)`
capture is void (x ends up data-less and *x reads whatever was referenced last).
